This project is a Task Management Dashboard built using React and Tailwind CSS. It allows users to create, manage, and organize their daily tasks efficiently.

Main Functionalities:
Add Task
Users can create a new task by entering a title and description using a form.
Edit Task
Existing tasks can be edited. When the user clicks the edit button, the form opens with pre-filled data.
Delete Task
Completed tasks can be removed from the list.
Mark Task as Complete
Users can mark tasks as completed. Completed tasks are shown separately.
Task Filtering
Tasks can be filtered based on:
All tasks
Completed tasks
Incomplete tasks
Search Functionality
Users can search tasks by title using the search bar.
Date Filter
Tasks can be filtered by selecting a specific date from the calendar.
Local Storage Support
All tasks are saved in the browser’s local storage, so data remains even after refreshing the page.
Dark/Light Theme Toggle
Users can switch between light mode and dark mode.
Responsive Design
The layout adjusts for mobile and desktop screens, including a hamburger menu for smaller devices.
User Profile Section
Displays user information like name, email, and profile image.
Modal Form UI
Task form appears as a popup modal for better user experience.
Context API Usage
Global state management is handled using React Context API to share data across components.